# 0112b WIP: EP2 RX diagnostics only, no data-path or buffer change.
#
# 0112 got the RX path working for one full packet and for one full packet
# followed by a short packet, but a host transfer containing two full
# 64-byte packets (128/129/130B) failed.  The focused test mixed failing
# lengths on the same endpoint, so its later samples are contaminated and
# the exact stuck GPD was never observed.
#
# This version changes no RX buffer, GPD layout, queue depth or TX code.  It
# adds the observability and clean-reset hooks needed to identify the real
# failure before choosing a fix:
#   - vendor IN 0xC0/0x24 returns the raw current GPD (dw0/next/buffer/dw3),
#     the previous and next GPD dw3, the full HWO bitmap, RX2CSR0/1/2,
#     RQCPR2/RQHIAR2/RQCSR2, zlp_err and the stall flag;
#   - vendor IN 0xC0/0x26 resets the RX ring, counters and endpoint for a
#     clean per-length test (stop RQCSR2, W1C SENTSTALL, EP_RST bit 2,
#     restore RX2CSR/QCR/RQERRIES/start address, re-arm and START);
#   - CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT, 0x02) is handled and uses the same reset
#     without clearing counters, so a host pipe clear does not leave the RX
#     endpoint wedged;
#   - RX2CSR0 SENTSTALL is latched in the stall flag, and ZLP errors are
#     counted instead of being silently cleared.
#
# The host harness must reset before every length, stop after an error, and
# read 0xC0/0x24 immediately; lengths 64/65/127/128/129/130 are tested one
# at a time.  The stuck GPD's dw3 high nibbles tell whether the hardware
# length write clobbers next_high/buffer_high (36-bit extension); RX2CSR0
# tells whether the endpoint really STALLed; zlp_err tells whether the host
# appended a ZLP.  No 128-byte buffer workaround is included.

MACOS_VERSION=13.5
KERNEL_CONFIG=DEVELOPMENT
MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET

BASE_REPO=https://github.com/MakrSas/ios-topaz.git
BASE_SHA=5095ac19dbdcf37b64b81fe443f4027ad51b84bf
PATCHSET_SHA256=b4755622e2ac2ac0d4776946888a0c142b5f2fc1a06f7b52eed8b881d592fc37
BASELINE_CHANGES_SHA256=1edb66332bb4daa8b1abcd6c4de77a0e88ed9c7e9bb4a2a7045a2696e53ab338

DXB_REPO=https://github.com/blacktop/darwin-xnu-build
DXB_SHA=663906528d1cd5ea8fde7de6f16de73db9511549

KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=
CI_RUN_ID=
CI_KERNEL_SHA256=
CI_KERNEL_EXEC_DATA_SHA256=
CI_IMAGE_SHA256=

BOOT_CMDLINE=config/0112b-boot.cmdline
